  "limitations": [
    "Only actual fixed Core Arc, fixed Vec<Option<Message>> and std mutex PAL are funded in this queue slice. Request/future/Span/Waker targets and errors remain independently owned.",
    "Original construction uses the existing eight response-cell permits and the same StockCore. No additional queue quota, count grant, wallet or authority is introduced.",
    "Actual System allocation/free oracles cover constructor identities and panic cleanup. Ready/EOF/deadline is not proof of physical exit. External test pins are not TaskCell claims.",
    "Waker reentry tests prove queue callbacks only. Tokio Semaphore waiter clone/close still call user Wakers while holding its own waitlist lock; readiness audit is read-only and has no runtime claim.",
    "Unrestricted Buffer clones can each create a readiness Box. Closed poll_ready can return arbitrarily many retained Box<ServiceError> without acquiring one of the eight cell positions; a payload owner does not prove the outer Box heap has exited.",
    "The MPSC block-peak audit did not establish a numerical physical bound or an infinite-growth counterexample. Ordinary MPSC is retained; no universal MPSC unboundedness assertion is made.",
    "Compiled negatives precede comment-only and additional test edits; per-negative source hashes and byte-exact restoration are preserved. Final source pins describe the final tested candidate.",
    "No new production unsafe. Unchanged oneshot Miri remains prior-checkpoint evidence and is not rerun or extrapolated to the queue or full Native graph.",
    "This refreshed stock does not close the whole Native 2 MiB graph, DNS/TLS/socket/auth/runtime backing, complete scalar source/producer or FE behavior.",
    "P04 executing, P05-P10 open, V1 None, Scalar Host gate closed. DNS and nested scalar accounting decisions remain pending.",
    "No final full SQL/default System/Linux/release performance/M07 completion claim. Linux testing is user-owned. No push, PR or archive."
  ],
